<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Per-item overrides for R4's material basis (R4MaterialCostExtension).

  Intentionally empty. Uncraftable gear (no costList, not made from stuff) is handled
  by R4's automatic MarketValue + techLevel fallback, which for the notable cases —
  the ultratech melee weapons (monosword / zeushammer / plasmasword / eltex staff,
  all MarketValue 2000) and the eltex apparel — already lands close to a sensible
  hand-tuned cost. So nothing needs an override today.

  This file is kept as a scaffold: add an R4MaterialCostExtension here only when the
  fallback reads poorly for a specific item and you want to hand-author its cost. The
  extension's <materials> is treated exactly like a costList and drives recycle, repair,
  and clean alike. Wrap DLC-only targets in a PatchOperationFindMod so absent DLC never
  logs a failed xpath. Template:

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Royalty</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="MeleeWeapon_MonoSword"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <li Class="RRRR.R4MaterialCostExtension">
          <materials>
            <Plasteel>40</Plasteel>
            <ComponentSpacer>3</ComponentSpacer>
          </materials>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>
-->
<Patch>
</Patch>
